<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12055" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπηλεγ-έως</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without caring for anything,
				outright, bluntly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> only in phrase 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῦθον ἀπηλεγέως ἀποειπεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.309
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.373
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πεπύθοιτο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1469
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νίσσετ᾽ ἀπηλεγέως</span>”
				<i>straightforwards, without looking about,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					1.785
				</span></i>
			; <i>sternly,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				4.687
			</span></i>; prob.
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνηλ-</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				1.226
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπηλεγές</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				495
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				2.510
			</span></i>. (From <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέγω,</span>
			
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νηλεγής, ἀνηλεγής.</span>
			)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
